<content><![CDATA[<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>
<multiple-choice question="In three-point lighting, which light is the main source that defines the subject's form?" single-option="" randomize="">
  <input type="checkbox" value="The key light" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="The fill light">
  <input type="checkbox" value="The rim (back) light">
  <input type="checkbox" value="The ambient light">
</multiple-choice>
<true-false-question question="An HDRI can light a whole scene and also provide realistic reflections.">
  <input type="checkbox" value="True" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="False">
</true-false-question>
<self-check title="Think it through">
  <p slot="question">How would you change a scene's lighting to make it feel tense or mysterious rather than cheerful?</p>
  <p>Raise the contrast between key and fill, use harder shadows and a low or side angle, shift to cooler or more saturated colors, and leave parts of the scene in darkness, lit only by motivated sources.</p>
</self-check>
